### 2.7 Embodiment & physiology

Physiological fields:

\[
\Phi(t) = \{\phi_{\text{capacity}}(t), \phi_{\text{modulation}}(t), \phi_{\text{damage}}(t), \phi_{\text{load}}(t)\}
\]

Embodiment cost:

\[
\mathcal{F}_{\text{emb}}(z, a, \Phi) = c_{\text{compute}}(z) + c_{\text{action}}(a) + c_{\text{depletion}}(\Phi)
\]

Viability:

\[
\phi_{\text{capacity}}(t) > \theta_{\text{shutdown}} \quad \forall t
\]

Timescale hierarchy:

\[
\tau_{\text{capacity}} \gg \tau_{\text{modulation}} \gg \tau_{\text{computation}} \gg \tau_{\text{action}}
\]

**Use this when:**  
You want to model agents that can actually “run out” of themselves—fatigue, stress, collapse.

